    "rRNA_pseudogene": {
      "description": "An rRNA-derived locus that GENCODE types rRNA but that MGI classifies as a pseudogene, so it is not expected to produce functional rRNA whatever the GTF biotype says. Both members are here because the publisher contradicts itself about them, not because this curation judged them non-functional. One of the two matters far more than the other for read counting. Rn18s-rs5 is 1,849 bp where every other rRNA-derived locus in this annotation is at most 148 bp, and it is the locus routinely filtered as rRNA contamination from mouse single-cell data under its former name Gm42418. A caller that sums rRNA alone therefore leaves out the single largest source of rRNA-derived reads in mouse, which for that metric is likely the wrong choice.",
      "source": "MGI, consulted for every locus in this file through the mgi_id attribute of the GENCODE M39 GTF and MGI MRK_List2.rpt retrieved 2026-08-22; exactly two of the 356 resolve to marker type Pseudogene and feature type pseudogene. Rn5s-ps1 is MGI:99528, 5S RNA pseudogene 1, and the -ps suffix is MGI's own pseudogene marker. Rn18s-rs5 is MGI:107222, 18s RNA related sequence 5, formerly Gm42418, and MGI is not non-committal about it: it types the marker Pseudogene outright, unlike its siblings Rn18s-rs1 through rs7 which MGI types rRNA gene. Ensembl carries the contradiction in plain sight, serving both loci with biotype rRNA and an MGI-sourced description that says pseudogene.",
      "gene_ids": [
        "ENSMUSG00000119584.1",
        "ENSMUSG00000119925.1"
      ]
    },
    "Mt_rRNA": {
      "description": "A ribosomal RNA gene encoded by the mitochondrial genome, kept separate from nuclear rRNA so a caller can count mitochondrial and nuclear ribosomal signal independently. Both members are on chrM: mt-Rnr1 is the 12S rRNA and mt-Rnr2 is the 16S rRNA.",
      "source": "The Mt_rRNA gene_type of the GENCODE M39 GTF, which needed no adjustment here. Confirmed against MGI:102493 (mt-Rnr1, mitochondrially encoded 12S rRNA) and MGI:102492 (mt-Rnr2, mitochondrially encoded 16S rRNA), both typed rRNA gene.",
      "gene_ids": [
        "ENSMUSG00000064337.1",
        "ENSMUSG00000064339.1"
      ]
    }
  }
